  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2002-p7.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let the integers be \\(n-1,\\) \\(n,\\) \\(n+1.\\) Then \\((n-1)n(n+1)=8\\cdot3n,\\) so \\(n^2-1=24\\) and \\(n=5.\\)\n\nThe three integers \\(4,\\) \\(5,\\) \\(6\\) have squares summing to \\(16+25+36=77.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Call the integers \\(n-1,\\) \\(n,\\) \\(n+1\\); their product is \\(n^3-n\\) and their sum is \\(3n\\)",
        "\\(n^2-1=24,\\) so find \\(n\\) and then compute \\((n-1)^2+n^2+(n+1)^2\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
